@@ -0,0 +1,30 @@
+{
+  "tool": "built-in image_gen",
+  "reference_images": [],
+  "output_dimensions": [
+    1024,
+    1024
+  ],
+  "images": [
+    {
+      "file": "styles/209-undertale.png",
+      "prompt": "Generate one fresh 1024x1024 square image, entirely from text, with no reference images. Use case: stylized-concept. Style is the absolute priority: an authentic Undertale-like low-resolution indie RPG battle encounter screen, overwhelmingly black and white, drawn with chunky hard-edged pixel clusters at a very low native resolution and integer upscaling. Flat black void, no photographic realism, no smooth shading, no antialiasing. Composition: upper half contains two small charmingly awkward full-body pixel sprites in side-facing interaction: a woman sits sideways on a tiny cafe stool, shoulders hunched happily around a steaming coffee mug as she takes a sip; a quirky friendly long-legged coffee-pot monster stands opposite her. A little side table holds a clearly crescent-shaped croissant. Lower half contains a single large empty black battle box outlined in thin white pixels, a small vivid red pixel heart inside, and a few scattered white pixel projectiles. No menu words, numbers, letter-like marks, dialogue or typography anywhere. Woman: adult early 30s, shoulder-length curly auburn hair expressed as rusty pixel clumps, freckles as a few pixels, round tortoiseshell glasses expressed as blocky round dark-and-light rims, mustard-yellow knit sweater expressed as a compact ochre pixel block with tiny stitches. White line sprites, large amounts of black negative space, sparse mustard and auburn on the woman plus the red heart are the only chromatic accents. Naive offbeat anatomy and proportions dictated entirely by the retro game medium. The output must look like actual pixel game art, not an illustration or photo with a pixel filter. No text, captions, signatures, logos or watermarks.",
+      "source": "/Users/manuelbieh/.codex/generated_images/01a0e992-99b2-75e2-91f4-271b52cb2927/exec-d4000eb7-ce14-4982-a539-5f72c5781ca1.png"
+    },
+    {
+      "file": "styles/210-monument-valley.png",
+      "prompt": "Generate one fresh 1024x1024 square image, entirely from text, with no reference images. Use case: stylized-concept. An authentic Monument Valley-like impossible-architecture puzzle-game scene. Style dictates everything: distant orthographic isometric view, a complete sculptural maze of pastel geometric towers, arches, pale coral parapets and powder-blue staircases floating in a spacious pale lavender void. Stair flights link incompatible elevations in a convincing Escher-like visual paradox; bridges twist and reconnect to their own supports. Precise minimal geometric surfaces, matte smooth colors, delicately shaded faces, soft ambient occlusion, no outlines or photographic textures. Architecture occupies most of the composition, asymmetrically balanced with substantial calm negative space; the human is tiny, about one fifteenth of the frame height. On an impossible stair landing walks a petite stylized adult woman in her early 30s, pausing mid-step to enjoy a small coffee cup held near her mouth. She has simplified shoulder-length curly auburn hair, small round tortoiseshell glasses, subtle freckle dots and a mustard-yellow knit sweater, rendered in the game's extremely simplified doll-like geometric anatomy. A tiny white plate with a croissant sits nearby on the broad landing's parapet. Architectural optical illusion first, tiny warm narrative detail second. Pastel ivory, pale teal, blush coral and lavender; sweater is a small mustard accent. Dreamy silent game-level composition, never a realistic portrait. No text, captions, typography, UI, logos, signatures or watermarks.",
+      "source": "/Users/manuelbieh/.codex/generated_images/01a0e992-99b2-75e2-91f4-271b52cb2927/exec-91042cfb-385c-49d2-8d72-6ff79fbd66f6.png"
+    },
+    {
+      "file": "styles/211-infrared.png",
+      "prompt": "Generate one fresh 1024x1024 square image, entirely from text, with no reference images. Use case: photorealistic-natural. A convincing false-color infrared film photograph shot in a lush outdoor cafe garden, with the medium determining the entire scene and lighting. Wide environmental composition, unusually low camera position and a moderately wide lens looking past a round cafe table toward a seated woman reclining happily in a garden chair, her legs and the surrounding garden visible. Dense foliage and vines blaze luminous snowy white and pale pink; some leaves blush saturated rose. Above the garden, the sky is dramatically dark navy, almost black. Sunlit human skin glows pale alabaster with infrared light scattering; shadows and materials have believable distinctive spectral response. The woman is in her early 30s with curly auburn shoulder-length hair, visible freckles, round tortoiseshell glasses and a mustard-yellow knit sweater whose cloth responds naturally to the false-color palette. She savors a coffee, cup raised just below her smiling face, her gaze directed into the garden. A croissant on a small plate is nearby on the foreground table. Genuine analog infrared aesthetics: crisp leaf forms with gentle film halation, fine grain, eerie intense light and surreal spectral colors. Make this a coherent photograph made using infrared-sensitive film, not an ordinary color portrait with an applied pink overlay. Strong diagonal garden perspective, lots of radiant vegetation and a dark sky. No text, captions, logos, signatures or watermarks.",
+      "source": "/Users/manuelbieh/.codex/generated_images/01a0e992-99b2-75e2-91f4-271b52cb2927/exec-a2890d01-877a-432b-9e15-c5035fc8d3b6.png"
+    },
+    {
+      "file": "styles/212-holga.png",
+      "prompt": "Generate one fresh 1024x1024 square image, entirely from text, with no reference images. Use case: photorealistic-natural. An authentic imperfect Holga plastic toy-camera photograph on cross-processed 120 film, square frame. Very close spontaneous candid profile at a small cafe: a woman in her early 30s fills the right and upper part of the image, her curly auburn shoulder-length hair partly cropped at the top, leaning down to enjoy coffee with the cup just touching her lips. Freckles, round tortoiseshell glasses and her mustard-yellow knit sweater remain recognizable through the soft optical rendering. A buttery croissant rests nearby on the saucer in the near lower foreground, blurred by the cheap lens. Intimate off-center framing, slight accidental camera tilt, very little setting visible beyond an indistinct cafe wall. Let the actual toy-camera medium lead: strong uneven black corner vignetting encroaches into the picture, hazy central focus and pronounced edge blur, small focus errors, uncorrected plastic-lens distortion, saturated cross-processed mustard and brick-red highlights with dirty cyan/green shadows, coarse medium-format film grain, a ragged warm red-orange light leak down the left edge and a subtle fogged streak near the bottom. Exposure feels spontaneous, sunlit and imperfect, with blocked shadows and softly blown highlights. No glossy digital portrait clarity, no illustration, no artificial neat overlay border. It should look physically photographed with a Holga and imperfectly developed film. No text, captions, letters, logos, signatures, timestamps or watermarks.",
+      "source": "/Users/manuelbieh/.codex/generated_images/01a0e992-99b2-75e2-91f4-271b52cb2927/exec-87ea4e61-63b1-4e3c-823f-c184c625a096.png"
+    }
+  ]
+}

